    <string name="mode_three_tier">Three-tier (default)</string>
    <string name="mode_three_tier_short">Three-tier</string>
    <string name="mode_three_tier_desc">AI and the approved Home list → cloud → your Home broadband. Video → cloud. Chinese apps, browsing, LAN and everything else use your own network directly.</string>
    <string name="mode_stable">Stable — everything via cloud</string>
    <string name="mode_stable_short">Stable</string>
    <string name="mode_stable_desc">AI → Home as above; every other public destination leaves through the cloud. LAN stays local.</string>
    <string name="mode_applies">Changes apply immediately to the running tunnel.</string>
    <string name="routing_scope_title">What Tono can and cannot recognise</string>
    <string name="routing_scope">Order: 21 cloud video exceptions → 166 AI / named Home entries (plus the Anthropic address range and the Claude, ChatGPT and Grok apps) → explicit cloud list → everything else direct. Matched traffic that fails is blocked, never retried directly; matched UDP/QUIC is refused so apps fall back to TCP. Apps using ECH, their own DNS-over-HTTPS, or cached addresses can hide an AI service; that traffic then goes direct. Unrecognised AI is not guaranteed to use Home.</string>
    <string name="routing_platform">On Android all apps, all TCP/UDP ports, IPv4 and IPv6 enter the tunnel. LAN, link-local and multicast stay outside. DNS for direct names uses your network\'s resolver; matched names never reach it. Hotspot clients and apps you exclude below bypass Tono entirely.</string>
